# Line endings
#
# The index is already 100% LF. Without this file, core.autocrlf=true (set on
# this clone) writes CRLF into the working tree on checkout, which is why git
# warns "LF will be replaced by CRLF" on every status. That matters beyond
# cosmetics: action/entrypoint.sh and scripts/*.sh are linted by shellcheck in
# CI and executed in a Linux container, where a CRLF shebang line fails.
#
# eol=lf pins the working tree to LF regardless of the local autocrlf setting,
# and text=auto normalises anything added in future. Both are no-ops against
# the current index.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must be LF even if someone sets autocrlf=input locally.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary: never diffed, never normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.db binary
*.pdf binary
